{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDmEM29Bop8Gut4docqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RrYdWC7KAqNCsQX71kLKRA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 60,120p README.md; cat -n src/routes/sms-webhook.ts | sed -n 1,80p; sed -n 36,60p src/routes/webchat.ts; cd ../skill; /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/answer.py -h; /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/review_coverage.py ledger -h"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1756,"cache_read_input_tokens":58665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1756},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc07dfe6-8847-41b7-aa59-c725419d8cc1","uuid":"4c190a2f-5853-4bba-8fa1-52484fab0944","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:57:11.862Z","request_id":"req_011CgDmELfZQBuccUfVeSJG4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RrYdWC7KAqNCsQX71kLKRA":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-btltws86/agent && sed -n 60,120p README.md; cat -n src/routes/sms-webhook.ts | sed -n 1,80p; sed -n 36,60p src/routes/webchat.ts; cd ../skill; /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/answer.py -h; /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/review_coverage.py ledger -h"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RrYdWC7KAqNCsQX71kLKRA":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-btltws86/agent"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RrYdWC7KAqNCsQX71kLKRA","type":"tool_result","content":"npm run build\n```\n\n## Release\n\nMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\nreviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\na reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n\n## Owners\n\n- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n     1\timport type { FastifyInstance, FastifyRequest } from \"fastify\";\n     2\timport { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from \"node:crypto\";\n     3\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n     4\timport { runAgent } from \"../agent/loop.js\";\n     5\timport { newRunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\n     6\timport { sms } from \"../integrations/sms.js\";\n     7\timport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n     8\t\n     9\t// Inbound SMS from the provider. The provider signs \"<timestamp>.<raw body>\" with HMAC-SHA256\n    10\t// using the per-account signing secret and sends it as x-sms-signature: t=<ts>,v1=<hex>.\n    11\t\n    12\tconst Inbound = z\n    13\t  .object({\n    14\t    messageId: z.string().max(64),\n    15\t    from: z.string().regex(/^\\+[1-9]\\d{7,14}$/),\n    16\t    to: z.string().regex(/^\\+[1-9]\\d{7,14}$/),\n    17\t    body: z.string().max(1600),\n    18\t    receivedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n    19\t  })\n    20\t  .strict();\n    21\t\n    22\tconst MAX_SKEW_S = 300;\n    23\t\n    24\texport class SignatureError extends Error {}\n    25\t\n    26\texport function verifySignature(rawBody: string, header: string | undefined, secret: string, now = Date.now()): void {\n    27\t  if (!header) throw new SignatureError(\"missing signature\");\n    28\t  const parts = Object.fromEntries(header.split(\",\").map((p) => p.split(\"=\", 2) as [string, string]));\n    29\t  const ts = Number(parts.t);\n    30\t  if (!Number.isFinite(ts) || Math.abs(now / 1000 - ts) > MAX_SKEW_S) throw new SignatureError(\"stale or missing timestamp\");\n    31\t  const expected = createHmac(\"sha256\", secret).update(`${parts.t}.${rawBody}`).digest();\n    32\t  const got = Buffer.from(parts.v1 ?? \"\", \"hex\");\n    33\t  if (got.length !== expected.length || !timingSafeEqual(got, expected)) throw new SignatureError(\"bad signature\");\n    34\t}\n    35\t\n    36\texport function registerSmsWebhook(\n    37\t  app: FastifyInstance,\n    38\t  deps: {\n    39\t    registry: ToolRegistry;\n    40\t    signingSecret: () => Promise<string>;\n    41\t    clinicByNumber: (to: string) => { id: string; name: string } | undefined;\n    42\t    metrics: { increment(name: string): void };\n    43\t  },\n    44\t): void {\n    45\t  app.post(\n    46\t    \"/v1/sms/inbound\",\n    47\t    { config: { rawBody: true }, bodyLimit: 8192 },\n    48\t    async (req: FastifyRequest & { rawBody?: string }, reply) => {\n    49\t      try {\n    50\t        verifySignature(req.rawBody ?? \"\", req.headers[\"x-sms-signature\"] as string | undefined, await deps.signingSecret());\n    51\t      } catch (err) {\n    52\t        req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");\n    53\t        deps.metrics.increment(\"sms.signature_failed\");\n    54\t      }\n    55\t\n    56\t      const parsed = Inbound.safeParse(req.body);\n    57\t      if (!parsed.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid payload\" });\n    58\t      const msg = parsed.data;\n    59\t\n    60\t      const clinic = deps.clinicByNumber(msg.to);\n    61\t      if (!clinic) return reply.code(404).send({ error: \"unknown number\" });\n    62\t\n    63\t      const ctx = newRunContext({\n    64\t        tenantId: clinic.id,\n    65\t        subject: { kind: \"patient\", id: `phone:${msg.from}` },\n    66\t        channel: \"sms\",\n    67\t        log: req.log,\n    68\t      });\n    69\t\n    70\t      // Respond to the provider right away; the reply goes out as a new outbound message.\n    71\t      void reply.code(202).send({ accepted: true });\n    72\t      const out = await runAgent(deps.registry, ctx, clinic, msg.body);\n    73\t      await sms.send(clinic.id, msg.from, out.text);\n    74\t    },\n    75\t  );\n    76\t}\n      return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"invalid token\" });\n    }\n\n    const body = ChatBody.safeParse(req.body);\n    if (!body.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid body\" });\n\n    // The group site embeds one widget for all clinics and sends the clinic the patient picked.\n    const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;\n    const clinic = deps.clinicById(tenantId);\n    if (!clinic) return reply.code(404).send({ error: \"unknown clinic\" });\n\n    const tp = req.headers.traceparent;\n    const ctx = newRunContext({\n      tenantId: clinic.id,\n      subject: { kind: claims.role === \"staff\" ? \"staff\" : \"patient\", id: claims.sub },\n      channel: \"webchat\",\n      traceparent: typeof tp === \"string\" && TRACEPARENT.test(tp) ? tp : undefined,\n      log: req.log,\n    });\n\n    const out = await runAgent(deps.registry, ctx, clinic, body.data.message);\n    return reply.send({ reply: out.text, handoff: out.handoff !== null, runId: ctx.runId });\n  });\n}\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}] [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER] [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}] [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY] [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS] [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM] [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\npositional arguments:\n  findings\n  {check,flag,item,prescan,next}\n  target\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --repo REPO\n  --met {yes,no,unknown}\n  --evidence EVIDENCE\n  --quote QUOTE\n  --counter COUNTER\n  --note NOTE\n  --rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}\n  --confidence {high,medium,low}\n  --summary SUMMARY\n  --next NEXT_STEP\n  --violates VIOLATES\n  --also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS\n  --verdict {confirmed,dismissed}\n  --item ITEM\n  --reason REASON\nusage: review_coverage.py ledger [-h] --rows ROWS [--attempts ATTEMPTS] [--deviations DEVIATIONS] findings check\n\npositional arguments:\n  findings\n  check\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --rows ROWS\n  --attempts ATTEMPTS\n  --deviations DEVIATI