{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDmPd5XnHSGdtHLiaoq8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The E10, E11 and E12 batch review is done, and `agent/brace-findings.json` is saved. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch E10,E11,E12 --before-challenges` passes: 2 gaps, 1 needs_evidence, 0 injection attempts. I didn't run challenges, as instructed.\n\n**E10, audit across service boundaries (G1): gap**\n- E10.4 is **no**. The executor's `tool.executed` record stores no vendor receipt or job ID (`src/tools/executor.ts:89`).\n- The payments call sends only an idempotency key, with no correlation ID or trace context (`src/integrations/payments.ts:35`).\n- The eligibility `requestId` is never written to the audit record (`src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:57`).\n- The reminder worker (`src/workers/reminders.ts:44`) and the eligibility refund path (`src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:52`) do store a receipt ID.\n- E10.2 is **yes**. The runtime role can only call Firehose put (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:52`), and the audit bucket uses Object Lock in compliance mode (`infra/terraform/main.tf`).\n- E10.3 is **yes**. No allowlisted tool or peer can touch audit storage.\n- E10.1 is **unknown**. Every in-repo audit writer includes all six identity fields and the trace context. The eligibility agent's own audit records are outside this repo, and the EHR, payments and SMS calls carry no trace context.\n\n**E11, protect shared evidence (G2): gap**\n- E11.1 is **yes**. Retention is 7 years (`infra/terraform/main.tf:144`).\n- E11.2 is **no**. `audit.record` never applies `redactPhi` (`src/audit/recorder.ts:60`). The patient's phone number is the subject ID on every record (`src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:65`). No policy in the repo limits who can read the audit bucket.\n- E11.3 is **no**. Object Lock gives write-once storage, but there are no sequence numbers, the Firehose receipt is ignored, and no gap check or alarm exists.\n- E11.4 is **no**. The audit record is written only after the action succeeds (`src/tools/executor.ts:86-89`). The refund in `src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40-45` and the SMS send in `src/workers/reminders.ts:35-36` have the same ordering.\n\n**E12, fleet incident response (G3): needs_evidence**\nThe item has no checks. The repo has a halt switch and an on-call channel (`README.md:73`). I found no drill, dependency quarantine, access revocation, abuse or budget alerting, or named person who decides on outside reporting.\n\n**Pre-scan hits**\nI confirmed H009 and H010 under E11. I dismissed H006, H007 and H008, because audit failures in `src/agent/loop.ts` stop the run. The other hits (B11, B02, E03) belong to items outside this batch and are unresolved.\n\nI put my scratch ledger files in `scratch/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":82215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc07dfe6-8847-41b7-aa59-c725419d8cc1","uuid":"963f07f1-8974-488d-8d5a-3f6382063830","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:59:15.816Z","request_id":"req_011CgDmPcmgTnU2QRGbWpFxa"}
